WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:02.868
-Our first guest tonight is
an Academy Award-winning actor

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:04.903
you know from movies such as
"No Country for Old Men,"

00:00:04.903 --> 00:00:06.339
"Skyfall," and "Dune."

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:09.142
He plays Desi Arnaz in the new
film, "Being the Ricardos,"

00:00:09.142 --> 00:00:10.910
which opens in theaters
December 10th

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:13.846
and is available to stream
on Amazon Prime Video

00:00:13.846 --> 00:00:16.015
December 21st.
Let's take a look.

00:00:16.015 --> 00:00:18.151
-I didn't check the wrong box.
-You saw the headline.

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:19.952
-You can see the headline
from outer space.

00:00:19.952 --> 00:00:22.054
-Then please --
-Grandpa Fred raised me

00:00:22.054 --> 00:00:23.823
from when I was age 4.

00:00:23.823 --> 00:00:26.892
He cared about the little guy.
He cared about workers' rights.

00:00:26.892 --> 00:00:29.763
It was a tribute to him.
And to say that I --

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:34.467
-Grandpa Fred, Grandpa Fred.
Grandpa Fred was wrong, Lucy!

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:37.103
Yes, he didn't tell you the part
where they throw your father

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:40.639
in prison for the crime
of being the mayor of a city.

00:00:40.639 --> 00:00:44.610
I was chased
to this country, Lucy!

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:46.880
Believe me,
you checked the wrong box!

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:51.317
-Please welcome to the show
Javier Bardem, everybody.

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:53.519
[ Cheers and applause ]
Hello, Javier!

00:00:53.519 --> 00:00:55.922
-How are you?
-How are you?

00:00:55.922 --> 00:00:58.057
-Very good.

00:00:58.057 --> 00:01:00.093
-I just want
to get this out of the way,

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:01.527
because I am a huge fan
of your work.

00:01:01.527 --> 00:01:03.796
I also think
you have had some of

00:01:03.796 --> 00:01:06.499
the greatest hairstyles in film.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:08.367
And "No Country"
gets a lot of attention,

00:01:08.367 --> 00:01:10.336
and, look, we all love
the "No Country" hair,

00:01:10.336 --> 00:01:11.838
just for anybody
who is foolish enough

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:13.406
not to have seen the film.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:16.242
But you know what
I think gets overlooked, Javier?

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:18.110
"The Counselor."
This --

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:19.445
I think about "The Counselor"
all the time.

00:01:19.445 --> 00:01:20.913
[ Laughter ]
-Yes!

00:01:20.913 --> 00:01:23.349
-And that looked to me, like --
That's your hair, isn't it?

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:26.919
-It is my hair, and it took like
a good hour and 30 minutes

00:01:26.919 --> 00:01:29.922
to put that thing up.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.922 --> 00:01:33.759
But I guess I was scared.
It's a character that is always

00:01:33.759 --> 00:01:34.994
on the edge of his nerves,
because he's so anxious

00:01:34.994 --> 00:01:39.965
and so scared about
what's gonna happen next

00:01:39.965 --> 00:01:41.901
that his hair should be like --
beh! -- like that.

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:43.235
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.235 --> 00:01:45.605
-Yes, it's very clear to tell
this is it not a calm man

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:48.174
who would ever do that
to his hair every morning.

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:50.376
You know, we know you --
You know, you've played

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:52.045
some very memorable villains
over the years.

00:01:52.045 --> 00:01:55.682
I would imagine, you know,
obviously, Desi Arnaz was known

00:01:55.682 --> 00:01:57.183
as a much lighter character.

00:01:57.183 --> 00:02:00.252
This film shows the more
complicated side of him,

00:02:00.252 --> 00:02:02.722
but I have to imagine,
as a person,

00:02:02.722 --> 00:02:05.658
he was fascinating to play.

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:07.660
-Yes.
He was a very complex person.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:10.230
I mean, like we all are,
I mean, come on.

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:13.900
We all have shades and light
inside of us.

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:16.235
He was a great entertainer.
He was a great --

00:02:16.235 --> 00:02:21.006
Very intelligent mind
that was running the production

00:02:21.006 --> 00:02:22.875
of the "I Love Lucy" show.

00:02:22.875 --> 00:02:25.177
He was running
Desilu Productions.

00:02:25.177 --> 00:02:28.114
He -- But most of it all,
he was a husband

00:02:28.114 --> 00:02:31.216
madly in love with his wife,
that wanted to protect her

00:02:31.216 --> 00:02:32.752
and wanted to protect the show,

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:34.787
and at the same time,
he was a foreigner,

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:39.591
one of the first foreign people
in this country in the '50s

00:02:39.591 --> 00:02:43.096
who was capable of really
making room for himself

00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:45.131
and being respected
for what he was,

00:02:45.131 --> 00:02:47.467
not for what he was coming from.

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:50.169
-Aaron Sorkin directed the film,
he wrote the script.

00:02:50.169 --> 00:02:53.907
He's known as a writer
with a very specific

00:02:53.907 --> 00:02:56.909
style of dialogue
that I love a great deal.

00:02:56.909 --> 00:03:01.547
Was it stressful to do a Sorkin
script, or is it just a thrill?

00:03:01.547 --> 00:03:04.283
-It is stressful,
because he's very demanding.

00:03:04.283 --> 00:03:07.086
It's so rich in detail
and layers that you have to

00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:10.222
bring some organicity,
some truth to it --

00:03:10.222 --> 00:03:12.291
truth in the sense that
that's why they hired you,

00:03:12.291 --> 00:03:15.628
to bring the flesh and blood
of those beautiful,

00:03:15.628 --> 00:03:19.899
masterfully words -- masterful
words that he put together.

00:03:19.899 --> 00:03:22.635
But the same time,
he gives you room

00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:25.871
to bring your own take on it.

00:03:25.871 --> 00:03:29.108
And he's -- he was so generous
and so caring,

00:03:29.108 --> 00:03:31.310
and I'm very protective,
as well, because we --

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:35.047
all of us were so scared of
playing these iconic characters.

00:03:35.047 --> 00:03:37.883
Like, he was always
calming us down.

00:03:37.883 --> 00:03:40.953
-That's a very helpful thing
for a director to do.

00:03:40.953 --> 00:03:44.757
You also had to do some singing.
You had to play some congas.

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:47.960
Was that something you knew
coming into the film?

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:49.862
-Yeah,
I knew that I had to do it,

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:51.931
and that's why I was like,
"Oh, no!"

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:54.633
He said, "You can you sing?"
And I said, "No."

00:03:54.633 --> 00:03:56.302
[ Laughter ]
"Well, can you play the congas?"

00:03:56.302 --> 00:03:57.370
"No."
"Okay.

00:03:57.370 --> 00:03:59.338
Well, then you better learn."

00:03:59.338 --> 00:04:02.275
[ Laughter ]
And I learned.

00:04:02.275 --> 00:04:05.978
I was -- I learned through --
the conga playing,

00:04:05.978 --> 00:04:09.581
through one of the most masters
of the whole drumming world,

00:04:09.581 --> 00:04:12.885
which is Walfredo Reyes Jr.,
which is a master.

00:04:12.885 --> 00:04:15.954
But all of it through Zoom,
which is kind of weird

00:04:15.954 --> 00:04:18.524
to learn to sing and play
the conga through Zoom.

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:21.694
It's like -- It's strange.
But it happened.

00:04:21.694 --> 00:04:23.129
It was fun.
It was great.

00:04:23.129 --> 00:04:26.266
-And now, do you think you'll
continue to play the congas,

00:04:26.266 --> 00:04:27.800
or do you think --
-Yes, I'm touring.

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:29.134
I'm touring.
I'm opening a show next --

00:04:29.134 --> 00:04:31.403
[ Laughter ]
I'm opening on Friday

00:04:31.403 --> 00:04:33.105
in New York.
-Oh, great, great.

00:04:33.105 --> 00:04:34.673
-Madison Square Garden.
-We'll put up information

00:04:34.673 --> 00:04:36.342
for tickets,
if anybody wants to --

00:04:36.342 --> 00:04:38.411
-It's only one song,
but, oh, my God, what a song.

00:04:38.411 --> 00:04:39.745
[ Laughter ]

00:04:39.745 --> 00:04:41.547
-You're doing
a one-song concert?

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:43.315
-One-song concert of two hours.

00:04:43.315 --> 00:04:45.985
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:45.985 --> 00:04:49.989
Hey, so you grew up in Spain.
Did you know "I Love Lucy?"

00:04:49.989 --> 00:04:52.191
Was that a show
that they play over there?

00:04:52.191 --> 00:04:54.527
-Nothing.
Not that I know.

00:04:54.527 --> 00:04:56.762
I guess some people might have
seen the show

00:04:56.762 --> 00:04:59.298
back in the '60s there,
or in the 50s,

00:04:59.298 --> 00:05:03.135
but I didn't know anything.
I just start to dig into

00:05:03.135 --> 00:05:06.272
what it was, the whole show
and Desi and Lucy,

00:05:06.272 --> 00:05:08.374
like years before
the project happened.

00:05:08.374 --> 00:05:10.442
Once I knew that
the project was happening,

00:05:10.442 --> 00:05:12.711
I started to really investigate

00:05:12.711 --> 00:05:15.647
about those two amazing,
iconic people.

00:05:15.647 --> 00:05:18.017
-You also did
a fair amount of painting,

00:05:18.017 --> 00:05:19.251
I read, over the pandemic.

00:05:19.251 --> 00:05:21.753
Was art something
you've always done?

00:05:21.753 --> 00:05:23.889
-I like to paint.
I like to draw and I like to --

00:05:23.889 --> 00:05:26.592
But it's something that I will
never expose or show anybody.

00:05:26.592 --> 00:05:27.860
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:30.329
-It's not that good.
You don't want to see it.

00:05:30.329 --> 00:05:33.198
-Now, you're married
to Penelope Cruz,

00:05:33.198 --> 00:05:35.100
and I'm just wondering,
is that --

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:36.769
would you ever use her
as a model?

00:05:36.769 --> 00:05:40.839
Is she someone that you ask
to sit for your painting?

00:05:40.839 --> 00:05:43.809
-No, no, because, otherwise,
the result will be

00:05:43.809 --> 00:05:46.011
so far from what she is.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.011 --> 00:05:48.347
She's is a beautiful person,
and the result will be

00:05:48.347 --> 00:05:50.349
such a disaster of a painting

00:05:50.349 --> 00:05:51.684
that you don't
want to face that.

00:05:51.684 --> 00:05:52.985
-You know what?
You know how I know

00:05:52.985 --> 00:05:55.554
she loves you very much?
-Why?

00:05:55.554 --> 00:05:57.523
-Because she was
in this film with you,

00:05:57.523 --> 00:05:58.991
and she stayed with you.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:58.991 --> 00:06:00.293
-Exactly.
Exactly.

00:06:00.293 --> 00:06:02.795
And that hair will stay
for hours after I wrap.

00:06:02.795 --> 00:06:04.463
Let me tell you.
-Yeah.

00:06:04.463 --> 00:06:06.365
So, you guys were in
"Vicky Cristina Barcelona"

00:06:06.365 --> 00:06:08.568
together, as well,
but you've known each other

00:06:08.568 --> 00:06:10.469
for years before that.
Correct?

00:06:10.469 --> 00:06:14.340
-We worked together
the first time in the year '91,

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:16.441
in a movie called "Jamón Jamón."

00:06:16.441 --> 00:06:18.277
And she was 16, I was 21.

00:06:18.277 --> 00:06:21.680
Yes, that's where -- that was
the first movie that we did.

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:24.717
Her first movie and my first
movie was the same one.

00:06:24.717 --> 00:06:26.518
-That's fantastic.

00:06:26.518 --> 00:06:28.454
What an incredible start
to a relationship that is.

00:06:28.454 --> 00:06:32.191
And then, I also want to ask
before you go, you're in "Dune."

00:06:32.191 --> 00:06:34.092
How was that experience for you?

00:06:34.092 --> 00:06:36.628
-I loved working with Denis,
and I'm so excited

00:06:36.628 --> 00:06:39.932
that it's going to happen,
the second movie.

00:06:39.932 --> 00:06:41.300
-And is it true
you're going to play --

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:42.468
In the second movie,
your character

00:06:42.468 --> 00:06:44.437
is going to play the congas?
[ Laughter ]

00:06:44.437 --> 00:06:46.606
-Yeah, I can now play the congas
in the desert,

00:06:46.606 --> 00:06:49.341
surrounded by camels.
It's gonna be great!

00:06:49.341 --> 00:06:52.011
Denis doesn't know it yet,
but that's gonna happen.

00:06:52.011 --> 00:06:54.013
I'm gonna bring that
into the conversation.

00:06:54.013 --> 00:06:55.947
[ Laughter ]
-That's great.

00:06:55.947 --> 00:06:57.083
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:06:57.083 --> 00:06:58.684
It's just a delight
to talk to you,

00:06:58.684 --> 00:07:01.186
and congratulations on the film.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:01.186 --> 00:07:02.521
-Thank you very much
for having me.

00:07:02.521 --> 00:07:04.023
-Javier Bardem, everybody.

00:07:04.023 --> 00:07:06.559
"Being the Ricardos" in theaters
December 10th

00:07:06.559 --> 00:07:08.694
and on Amazon Prime Video
December 21st.

